//api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/deployments","created_at":"2018-11-27T03:35:03Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T09:08:20Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-10T20:45:00Z","git_url":"git://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy","homepage":"https://www.sqlalchemy.org","size":99269,"stargazers_count":11252,"watchers_count":11252,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1606,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":205,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["python","sql","sqlalchemy"],"visibility":"public","forks":1606,"open_issues":205,"watchers":11252,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the use case\n\nSince [PostgreSQL 14.0](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/14.0), HSTORE values can be accessed using square brackets in addition to the `->` operator:\n\n```sql\nSELECT store['key'] FROM my_table;\nSELECT store -> 'key' FROM my_table;  -- exactly equivalent\n```\n\nBut contrary to `->`, this syntax can be used in UPDATE statements:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE my_table SET store['key'] = 'value';  -- ✅ works as expected\nUPDATE my_table SET store -> 'key' = 'value';  -- ❌ ERROR: syntax error at or near \"->\" \n```\n\nSQLAlchemy currently always use `->`, which means that that the following MRE emits invalid SQL:\n\n```py\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, MetaData, Table, update\nfrom sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import HSTORE, dialect\n\nmy_table = Table(\"my_table\", MetaData(), Column(\"store\", HSTORE()))\n\nstmt = update(my_table).values({my_table.c.store[\"key\"]: \"value\"})\nprint(stmt.compile(dialect=dialect()))  # ❌ UPDATE my_table SET store -> %(store_1)s=%(param_1)s\n```\n\nJust updating `HSTORE.Comparator._setup_getitem` to use `operators.getitem` make it works:\n\n```py\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, MetaData, Table, update\nfrom sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import HSTORE, dialect\nfrom sqlalchemy.sql import operators\n\nHSTORE.comparator_factory._setup_getitem = lambda self, ix: (operators.getitem, ix, self.type.text_type)\n\nmy_table = Table(\"my_table\", MetaData(), Column(\"store\", HSTORE()))\n\nstmt = update(my_table).values({my_table.c.store[\"key\"]: \"value\"})\nprint(stmt.compile(dialect=dialect()))  # ✅ UPDATE my_table SET store[%(store_1)s]=%(param_1)s\n```\n\nWould you be open to change this, probably opt-in to not break PostgreSQL <14? (eg via `HSTORE(use_subscription=True)` or similar option)\n\n### Databases / Backends / Drivers targeted\n\nPostgreSQL 14+, all drivers\n\n### Example Use\n\nSee MRE above, or using ORM equivalent versions that currently do not work:\n\n```py\nsession.query(MyTable).update({MyTable.store[\"key\"]: \"value\"})\nsession.execute(update(MyTable).values({MyTable.store[\"key\"]: \"value\"}))\n```\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/12948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/12948/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]